        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="infra-81" edge="1" parent="1" source="infra-27" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;startArrow=block;startFill=1;strokeColor=#66B2FF;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=1;dashPattern=6 4;exitX=0.8408256880733945;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;fontSize=10;fontColor=#333333;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" target="infra-70" value="peering">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="infra-82" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#666666;" value="Peering is hub-to-spoke only: no spoke-to-spoke peering." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="20" width="330" x="245" y="750" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="infra-83" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;absoluteArcSize=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FAFAFA;strokeColor=#4C4C4C;strokeWidth=1.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;fontColor=#333333;" value="&lt;b&gt;How the path is enforced&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1 · Routes.&lt;/b&gt; Each spoke sends 0.0.0.0/0 and 10.100.0.0/14 to the NVA. Azure&#39;s own 0.0.0.0/0 → Internet route then shows as Invalid. A reachability assertion checks this on every tier after each apply (assert.yml, 9 checks).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2 · Tier 2 → tier 0 is blocked twice.&lt;/b&gt; On the NVA (nftables drop) and on the tier-0 NSG (DenyTier2ToTier0). Evidence S2 opened one layer at a time: the NSG held while the NVA was open.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3 · On-premises over BGP.&lt;/b&gt; The spokes have no on-prem route of their own; traffic follows the default route to the NVA, and FRR on the NVA sends it into ipsec0. A self-hosted NVA cannot inject BGP routes into the Azure fabric, so they live in FRR and the kernel on both gateways." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="215" width="450" x="1210" y="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="infra-84" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;absoluteArcSize=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FDECEC;strokeColor=#C62828;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;fontColor=#333333;" value="&lt;b&gt;Tested drift (evidence Q1)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The tier-1 subnet was detached from its route table outside Terraform. The table and both routes still existed, so every plan-time check passed, yet tier 1 was reaching the Internet directly, past the NVA. The assertion failed on exactly tier 1; the next apply restored the association." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="100" width="450" x="1210" y="315" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="infra-85" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;absoluteArcSize=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#9E9E9E;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=1;dashPattern=6 4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;fontColor=#333333;" value="&lt;b&gt;Reserved, not built&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;AzureFirewallSubnet and GatewaySubnet stay in the address plan. A time-boxed window with the managed Azure Firewall is decided on 23 Nov. The managed VPN Gateway window was dropped (ADR D19)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="80" width="450" x="1210" y="450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="infra-86" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;absoluteArcSize=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#2E7D32;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;fontColor=#333333;spacingRight=52;" value="&lt;b&gt;rg-cne-observability&lt;/b&gt; · persistent&lt;br&gt;Flow logs on all 5 VNets and the NVA&#39;s logs go here. See page 3, Telemetry &amp;amp; detection." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="450" x="1210" y="550" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="infra-87" parent="1" style="image;aspect=fixed;html=1;points=[];verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#333333;image=img/lib/azure2/analytics/Log_Analytics_Workspaces.svg;imageBackground=none;" value="" vertex="1">
